# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so a fresh clone
# rewrites text files to CRLF in the working tree. Git Bash tolerates that in a
# shell script, but /bin/sh on Linux does not — a CRLF script fails with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M". That bites when the scripts below are run from
# WSL, from a container, or by a collaborator on macOS or Linux.
#
# Deliberately narrow: no blanket `* text=auto`, which would renormalise every
# file in the repository at once and bury real changes in whitespace churn.

*.sh            text eol=lf
.githooks/*     text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerignore  text eol=lf
nginx.conf      text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
